{"id": "unknown-2026-11-22-007", "date": "2026-11-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cathode_material", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Briggs & Stratton keeps the lights on longer with bigger 16 kWh LFP battery", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/08/gary_dark.png?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For decades, Briggs &amp; Stratton has helped keep the lights on after the storm with its gas-powered generators. Now, the company is bringing that legacy to the electric age with a new 16 kWh backup battery designed to scale with your growing energy needs.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"battery-storage,home-battery,s", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/22/briggs-stratton-keeps-the-lights-on-longer-with-bigger-16-kwh-lfp-battery/", "type": "rss"}]}
